+## Request 21: Duplicate customers
+**Status**: ✅ Completed and tested
+
+### What was done
+- Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` to src/customers.js
+- Returns ok({ customers, invoices }) with:
+  - fromId customer removed from customers array
+  - All invoices belonging to fromId reassigned to intoId
+- Errors:
+  - CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if either fromId or intoId not in customers
+  - SAME_CUSTOMER if both IDs refer to same customer
+- Features:
+  - Normalizes both IDs (trim and uppercase) for comparison
+  - Maintains immutability (returns new arrays, doesn't mutate inputs)
+  - Preserves invoice data while reassigning customerId
+  - Works with unnormalized input (spaces, mixed case)
+- Added SAME_CUSTOMER error code to src/errors.js
+- Added 11 comprehensive tests covering:
+  - Customer removal from array
+  - Invoice reassignment (one and multiple invoices)
+  - Normalized ID handling
+  - Missing customer errors (from and into)
+  - Same customer rejection (exact and normalized match)
+  - No mutation of original arrays
+  - Result immutability
+  - Multiple invoices with mixed customer origins
+  - Empty invoice arrays
